it's true that there's nothing quite  like a movie where you can download  kungfu directly into your brain but  there are plenty of other trippy amazing  films out there that you love if you're  a fan of the matrix since its released  the matrix really became the gold  standard of movies that asked how real  is our reality everyone who saw it had  to question the world at least for a  moment and wonder if everything we see  and feel everyday actually exists or if  it's all just an illusion there is no  spoon well folks let us assure you we're  not living in a simulation even if there  are some days where we'd actually prefer  to wake up in a goo pod and find out it  was all fake we've just got to make the  best of this reality because it's the  only one we have  or is it director Christopher Nolan's  2010 hit Inception raised this very  question and gave no satisfying answer  but in a very satisfying way starring  Leonardo DiCaprio Ellen Page Tom Hardy  and other superstars this film is packed  with great moments that will stick in  your memory forever even if the plot  leaves you scratching your head similar  to what the Wachowskis achieved with  their masterpiece trilogy the beautiful  filmmaking in Inception pushes the  boundaries of what audiences thought was  possible on the big screen the question  at the core of both Inception and the  matrix is something that's been  contemplated by children and  philosophers for centuries and it's an  idea that rolls around in our human  experience accompanying us our whole  lives  how can we know if what we experience as  reality is truth there's no way to know  for sure but hey if this is a dream a  simulation or some kid snowglobe at  least we've got some great movies to  watch if you've never heard of existence  and you give it a watch after this you  might be shocked that you'd never seen  it before but there's actually a reason  for its obscurity director David  Cronenberg's mind  bending body twisting action flick might  have been a major sci-fi hit but it was  unfortunate enough to be released only a  few weeks after the matrix and it's  similar themes were overshadowed by the  Wachowskis wildly popular visually  stunning blockbuster as a result  existence has flown under the radar as a  cult classic for years but now it's time  to give this film it's jus as one of the  best and trickiest films of the 90s  starring Jude Law and Jennifer Jason  Leigh existence is set in a near future  where game designers a massive  celebrities and the truth about the  world is more complicated than it first  appears this wild ride of the movie  thrills from start to finish with  Cronenberg's signature gross-out body  horror aesthetics some fun and weirdly  squishy shoot-'em-up action and two  compelling actors in its leading roles  it's a little bit darker than the matrix  and as hard as it might be to believe  it's a whole lot weirder to beyond that  though existence definitely has a  similar vibe to its more popular genre  cousin that will surely scratch the itch  when you just got to put more twisty  reality bending plot in your brain tell  the truth are we still looking fans who  love Keanu Reeves for the way that the  matrix redefined action movies for an  entire generation definitely know and  love these movies already if however you  somehow managed to miss the  bone-crushing  senses shattering dog-loving  shoot-'em-up action of John wick and its  sequels get ready for a wild ride Keanu  is at the helm of these hit action  movies starring as the title character  perform a hitman who leaves his old life  of violence behind to find peace with  his wife when the last remnants of his  civilian life are shattered by a group  of thugs who steal his car and kill his  dog John is ready for a fight or two or  200 basically it's the story of a man  who loved a woman  then who loved a dog and who then goes  on the most brutal brazen rampage ever  to grace the silver screen people keep  asking if I'm back and I haven't really  had an answer but now yeah I'm taking on  back John wick and its sequels are a  brutal love letter to fight scenes and  if you've got a taste for a bit of the  old ultraviolence we can guarantee this  is your jam behind the camera there's a  lot to love about this franchise as well  especially if you're a fan of Neos  adventures one of the best and most  prolific stunt people in the film  industry  Chad Stachowski is the director of John  wick along with David leech before  taking the directors gesture he'll ski  was a stunt double for Keanu Reeves in  the matrix and John wick relied on many  of the same stunt coordinators that  helped reinvent action movies back in  1999 plus Laurence Fishburne shows up in  the series as the Bowery King a  character whose every bit as mysterious  as Morpheus and might just be the key to  guiding Keanu through another ultra  violent reality if you love the  philosophical talking points and world  building law behind the story of The  Matrix we can pretty much guarantee that  you'll also love the Animatrix the  lesser-known fourth film in the saga  everyone remembers as a trilogy one of  the more unique entries on this list the  Animatrix is an anthology made up of  nine stories that take place inside and  outside the matrix set between the  Matrix Reloaded and the final events of  the Matrix Revolutions each story is  animated in a totally different style  making this film watchable all at once  or is a set of distinct pieces if that's  more your thing plus you'll see some  familiar faces and hear familiar voices  like neo and Trinity both voiced by  their original actors Keanu Reeves and  carrie-anne moss while it's often  overlooked this is a do not miss film  for any true matrix lover and if you had  the impression that it's just a cartoon  cash-in think again four of the short  films in this movie were written by  that would shall cease themselves  covering a wide array of tales and  emotions on both the human and robot  sides of the story the tales of the  Animatrix are varied in their things  some highlight the strange and simple  beauty of any world humans inhabit or  explore the indomitable will and spirit  the sets Humanity of heart some awesome  shorts fill out more of the history and  give a fuller picture of the world  before the robot uprising that  eventually led to humanity's underground  survival all in all it's a collection of  trippy and beautiful shorts that you  want to watch over and over again in  2008 the Wachowskis took a departure  from the tone of their mind-bending  Matrix trilogy with Speed Racer and used  their considerable talents to make a  bright colorful adventure that the whole  family could enjoy this is of course an  American adaptation of the beloved manga  turned anime series from the 60s and  while it was a woefully underrated  box-office bomb when it was released to  theaters it's absolutely worth watching  it's got all the gorgeous wachowski  visuals fun and fast-paced action  sequences and world-building through  visual design without all the doom and  gloom of a post-apocalyptic society  constantly on the brink of collapse in  addition to special effects that capture  the feeling of a pop art cartoon brought  to life Speed Racer boasts a  star-studded cast packed with fan  favorites like John Goodman Susan  Sarandon and Christina Ricci despite its  financial shortcomings Speed Racer has  become a cult classic and not just  because of its unique style the  over-the-top artificial look of its  world is paired with the sincerity at  the heart of its story that's rarely  been matched in a movie for kids or for  adults for that matter put it all  together and it's easy to see why it won  over the hearts and minds of millions of  fans since Plus this is a chimpanzee and  ninjas before the matrix explored the  idea of a digital world that existed  alongside reality that was Tron  incredibly stylish wildly fun a product  of pure imagination run wild  the 1982 original is another genre  defining film that paved the way for the  witch s keys to make them magic the big  difference is that rather than  discovering that they're trapped in a  false reality the designers and  programmers who get sucked into the  virtual world of Tron know they're  trapped in a simulation it's getting out  there could be deadly Disney's  cutting-edge cult classic stars Jeff  Bridges is Kevin Flynn a programmer  turned video game arcade owner turned  virtual warrior key Andy's buddies are  up against an artificial intelligence  seeking to increase its own power and  rule the world if that sounds familiar  it's because Tron most likely influenced  at least a few of the ideas behind the  matrix in both visuals and writing it  might be a movie for kids but Tron  explored philosophical ponderings about  the role of technology in our lives and  experimented with what at the time were  brand new advances of computer-generated  images as special effects with two  Academy Award nominations and a great  soundtrack Tron is a fantastic film that  stood the test of time it also got a  similarly underrated sequel in 2010 that  makes for an interesting watch if only  to see how its themes were treated  before and after the matrix redefined  these ideas for pop culture it's worth a  watch and as an added bonus you can brag  to your friends that you watched the  only film entirely inspired by the first  time its creator Steve and Liz Berger  saw the video game pong set in the  dystopian Neo Tokyo in the year 2019  Akira is a piece of art from start to  finish and even the most jaded adults  who think anime is only for kids will be  blown away by the gorgeous art and come  away effective from the masterful  storytelling originally when Akira was  released in 1988 in Japan movie didn't  make much of a splash it was released  the year after in the United States and  it picked up steam with critics and fans  alike today Akira is considered one of  the most important science fiction  movies ever made  not just in anime but in the entirety of  film it's also regarded as a landmark  piece of animation that set the bar for  generations to come  and  influenced thousands of other artists  and filmmakers including the Wachowskis  while it doesn't have the artificial  reality elements of the matrix the  mind-bending story centers around a  young man trying to save his friend from  a nefarious government plot plus there  are some extremely cool motorcycles that  will make you want to take to the  neon-lit open road and amazing character  design that will definitely fool you  into thinking it's a good idea to dress  in head-to-toe red leather if you only  see one movie on this list make it akira  ghost in the shell' the 1995 anime  inspired by a manga of the same name was  initially like many of the movies on our  list of box-office flop as we all  learned from Morpheus though sometimes  things are not as they seem today it's  considered one of the best science  fiction films of all time and it's  absolutely at the top of many best anime  lists as well though released in the  mid-90s ghost in the shell' is set in  the year 2029 in a cyberpunk Japan where  human lives are even more intimately  connected with the machines and  Technology around them than they are  today  following the life of a cyborg agent  specializing in taking down  technological threats this is a non-stop  action thriller where the pacing and  animation will keep you hooked all the  way from start to finish and just like  the matrix it does it all while posing  some serious philosophical questions  about the nature of man and machine it's  no secret that the groundbreaking anime  was a huge influence on the matrix as it  majorly inspired some of the thinking  and visuals of the Wachowskis film  exploring similar themes of identity and  its existence in relation to society  even if you don't want to spend time  pondering all that though you should  still watch it just for the mind-blowing  action sequences that feature animation  that has rarely been equalled check out  one of my new videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss  single one  [Music]
 

